s":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the first test case, $$$a = 3$$$, $$$b = 5$$$, and $$$c = 9$$$ satisfies the condition as $$$3 \\mathbin{\\&} 5 = 1$$$, $$$5 \\mathbin{\\&} 9 = 1$$$, and $$$3 \\mathbin{\\&} 9 = 1$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the second test case, $$$a = 7$$$, $$$b = 3$$$, and $$$c = 22$$$ satisfies the condition as $$$7 \\mathbin{\\&} 3 = 3$$$, $$$3 \\mathbin{\\&} 22 = 2$$$, and $$$7 \\mathbin{\\&} 22 = 6$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the third test case, it can be proven that there are no three non-negative integers $$$a$$$, $$$b$$$, and $$$c$$$ such that $$$a \\mathbin{\\&} b = 4$$$, $$$b \\mathbin{\\&} c = 8$$$, and $$$a \\mathbin{\\&} c = 12$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"document"},"index":"B","problemCode":"2153B","schema":2,"sourceKind":"html","sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/contest/2153/problem/B"}